        drivingExperience: "The 107hp ADW engine provides a very relaxed, unhurried driving experience. In the heavy A6 C4 chassis, it feels decidedly slow by modern standards, but the multi-point injection ensures it runs smoothly. It is best suited for comfortable, steady highway cruising rather than aggressive city driving or quick overtakes.",
        mechanicVerdict: "The ADW is an absolute tank of an engine. It is the definition of 'they don't build them like they used to.' The cast iron block is virtually indestructible. Your only enemies are electrical: replace the main ECU power relay, clean the Idle Stabilizer Valve, and ensure the distributor Hall sender is healthy. Fix the brittle vacuum lines, and this engine will happily reach half a million kilometers.",
