        drivingExperience: "The 163hp AEJ is the definition of a smooth, relaxed executive cruiser, albeit slightly slower than the standard AAH. It completely lacks the peaky, rev-happy nature of the 16V engines, instead relying on a buttery smooth, linear delivery of torque. In the heavy A6 C4 chassis, it is definitively slow, but it sounds excellent and provides a highly refined, whisper-quiet highway ride.",
        mechanicVerdict: "The AEJ 2.8 12V V6 is a robust engine that requires highly specific maintenance. You MUST use the proper cam locking bar to do the timing belt; 'mark and pray' mechanics will ruin the timing. Expect to reseal the entire top end (valve covers and valley pan) to cure the inevitable oil leaks. Fix the broken vacuum lines for the intake changeover valves, ensure the MAF is clean, and it will effortlessly cruise for 300,000+ kilometers.",
