        timingType: "Belt (Dual timing belt system. The front toothed belt drives the camshaft and water pump, while a separate rear toothed belt drives the Bosch VP37 injection pump. Highly reliable, but requires precise dynamic timing via VCDS after replacement)", injectionType: "Direct Injection (Bosch VP37 Electronic Rotary Distributor Pump. Mechanical injection with electronic quantity control. Legendary durability but sensitive to air leaks and timing drift)", engineLifespan: "500,000+ km (The cast-iron 5-cylinder 2.5 TDI is arguably one of the most indestructible diesel engines ever manufactured by Audi. It is common to see these engines outlive the chassis entirely)", turboType: "Wastegate Turbocharger (KKK K14. Simple, incredibly robust, and provides a distinct, old-school turbo whistle, though inherently laggy compared to modern VNT turbos)", ecuType: "Bosch MSA11 (An early 8-bit ECU. Diagnostic capabilities are primitive, and tuning requires physically desoldering and replacing EPROM chips)", euroStandard: "Euro 1 / Euro 2", maxPowerStockInternals: "250+ hp (The legendary I5 block is massively over-engineered. The bottom end easily handles double the factory power, limited only by airflow and fueling)",
