        timingType: "Belt (Dual timing belt system. The front toothed belt drives the camshaft and water pump, while a separate rear toothed belt drives the Bosch VP37 injection pump. Highly reliable, but requires precise dynamic timing via VCDS after replacement)", injectionType: "Direct Injection (Bosch VP37 Electronic Rotary Distributor Pump. Features highly desirable, larger .216mm injector nozzles straight from the factory, making it a favorite for tuners)", engineLifespan: "500,000+ km (The AEL is the holy grail of 90s Audi diesels. The cast-iron 5-cylinder block is utterly indestructible. High-mileage examples easily clear half a million kilometers with basic maintenance)", turboType: "Wastegate Turbocharger (KKK K14. Features specific mapping and slightly different A/R ratios compared to the AAT to flow more air for the 140hp output. Produces an iconic turbo whistle)", ecuType: "Bosch MSA11 (An early 8-bit ECU. Highly robust but requires physical chip desoldering/socketing to install aftermarket tunes)", euroStandard: "Euro 2", maxPowerStockInternals: "280+ hp (The legendary 5-cylinder block is massively over-engineered. The bottom end effortlessly handles double the factory power output, limited only by airflow, clutch, and fueling)",
        fuelConsumption: { city: "7.8 - 8.8 L/100km", highway: "5.2 - 6.0 L/100km", mixed: "6.5 - 7.2 L/100km", sporty: "8.5+ L/100km" },
