            drivingExperience: "The 150hp AWT in the A6 C5 is a highly refined commuter. Thanks to the fast-spooling K03 turbo and ME7.5 electronic throttle, power delivery is exceptionally smooth and lag-free, making it feel remarkably capable around town despite the heavy chassis. It is quiet and comfortable, though it loses breath quickly at high RPMs on the highway.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The AWT (06A block) is an excellent, highly tuneable engine, but it is less forgiving than the older AEB. You MUST use synthetic oil and stick to strict 8k-10k km intervals to prevent oil sludge from killing the engine. Swap out the problematic factory coil packs for R8 units, delete or upgrade the fragile PCV system, and it will be an incredibly loyal daily driver.",
            repairCostEstimate: "$400 - $800 / year (Factoring in PCV, coil packs, and oil maintenance)"
