            author: "2002 Audi RS6 Sedan (https://skfb.ly/oYA8I) by o1o6o is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).",
            drivingExperience: "The 180hp AJL 1.8T in the A6 C5 is a surprisingly punchy highway cruiser. It feels noticeably faster and more eager to rev than the standard 150hp variants. The 'Big Port' head provides a very linear power delivery that makes the heavy chassis feel lighter. The 5-valve head creates a sophisticated induction note at high RPMs, and when paired with a manual gearbox, it offers a genuinely engaging classic Audi feel.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The AJL is one of the greatest and rarest engines Audi ever built. It is a true 'old school' forged block that can handle triple its factory power right out of the box. However, it will absolutely not tolerate poor maintenance. If you buy one, immediately clean the oil pickup tube and swap the vacuum lines. Do that, and it is a 500,000 km engine.",
