                "Valvetrain Destruction (Timing Belt Snap) - This is a strictly interference engine. If the massive timing belt snaps due to an ignored 90,000 km interval, the pistons will simultaneously smash all 30 valves.",
                "Valvetrain Destruction (Chain Tensioner Failure) - If the rear cam chain tensioner pads break completely and the chain skips a tooth, catastrophic valve-to-piston contact will occur.",
                "Engine Fire Risk (Oil Leaks) - Because the V6 fills the engine bay entirely, severe oil leaks from the valve covers drip directly onto the blistering hot exhaust manifolds, causing noxious smoke and a legitimate fire hazard.",
                "Catalytic Converter Meltdown - Running rich from a failing MAF sensor or driving with a misfiring coil pack will dump raw fuel into the exhaust, quickly melting the dual ceramic catalytic converters.",
                "Heater Core Blockage/Rupture - A common C5 chassis issue. The heater matrix clogs with silicate sludge, resulting in no cabin heat, or bursts, leaking scalding coolant onto the floorboards.",
                "Automatic Transmission Failure - If paired with the 01V ZF 5HP19 automatic, ignoring the 80,000 km fluid change interval will lead to torque converter lockup clutch failure and valve body issues."
