            author: "2002 Audi RS6 Sedan (https://skfb.ly/oYA8I) by o1o6o is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).",
            drivingExperience: "The 136hp ALW 2.4 V6 is an incredibly smooth, but agonizingly slow executive cruiser. Because the ECU artificially chokes the power output, the engine feels totally breathless at higher RPMs. In the heavy A6 chassis, overtaking requires immense planning and patience. However, it sounds excellent and provides an incredibly quiet, comfortable highway ride.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The ALW 30V V6 is mechanically identical to its 165hp brothers, meaning it requires the exact same massive maintenance budget but rewards you with significantly less power. You MUST use the proper cam locking bar to do the timing belt. Expect to pay to reseal the entire top end (valve covers, cam seals, and valley pan) to cure the inevitable oil leaks. The absolute first thing any owner should do is get the ECU flashed to remove the 136hp factory restriction.",
