            timingType: "Belt & Chain (Primary toothed timing belt drives exhaust cams and water pump. Internal rear chains with hydraulic tensioners link intake cams. Tensioner guide pads require regular inspection).", injectionType: "Multi-Point Injection (Bosch Motronic sequential port fuel injection. This specific 156hp mapping was created for specific emissions or regional requirements, acting as a very slight detune of the standard 165hp version)", engineLifespan: "350,000+ km (The cast-iron V6 block is virtually indestructible under normal use. However, the engine's lifespan is frequently cut short by severe neglect of oil leaks, failing timing components, or catastrophic chain tensioner pad disintegration. With proper maintenance, it will easily outlast the chassis)", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. Relies entirely on the high-flowing 5-valve-per-cylinder head design and a dual-path variable intake manifold to generate a smooth, linear torque curve)", ecuType: "Bosch Motronic (A robust electronic management system with a slightly restricted map)", euroStandard: "Euro 3", maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The bottom end is immensely strong, sharing architecture with the larger 2.8L. However, making significant power naturally aspirated is impossible. Adding forced induction is cost-prohibitive)",
