    drivingExperience: "The 110hp AVG 1.9 TDI is a classic workhorse. The VNT turbo spools very early, providing a strong surge of low-end torque that makes the heavy A6 feel perfectly adequate in city traffic. It is noisy at idle but incredibly frugal on the highway, easily capable of 1000+ km on a single tank.",
    mechanicVerdict: "The AVG is an absolute legend of reliability. Yes, you will spend time chasing down vacuum leaks, cleaning the clogged EGR valve, and dealing with a sticking turbo actuator. But the core engine block, rods, and pistons are utterly bulletproof. It is a 500,000+ km engine that represents the peak of 90s diesel durability.",
