                timingType: "Chain (Complex rear-mounted timing chain system with four chains driving the camshafts and accessories. Servicing requires complete engine removal).", injectionType: "Direct Injection (FSI. Fuel is sprayed directly into the combustion chamber at high pressure. Highly prone to intake valve carbon buildup).", engineLifespan: "250,000+ km (The aluminum block is sensitive to oil starvation. This facelift version features the Audi Valvelift System, adding complexity. Longevity heavily depends on timing chain care and regular carbon cleaning).", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. Features Audi Valvelift System (AVS) on the intake valves for optimized breathing).", ecuType: "Siemens Simos 8.1", euroStandard: "Euro 5", maxPowerStockInternals: "280+ hp (Strong rotating assembly, but this detuned 190hp version is limited by ECU software and NA architecture).",
                fuelConsumption: { city: "11.5 - 12.5 L/100km", highway: "6.5 - 7.5 L/100km", mixed: "8.5 - 9.5 L/100km", sporty: "13.0+ L/100km" },
                oilSpecification: "VW 502.00 5W-40",
                commonIssues: [ 
                    "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Direct injection FSI engines do not wash the intake valves with fuel. Oil vapor bakes onto the valves, causing severe carbon choking, misfires, and rough idle.",
                    "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The complex chain system at the rear of the engine stretches over time, and the plastic guides break, causing a 'death rattle' on cold starts.",
                    "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: The cam-driven HPFP roller/follower can wear out, potentially damaging the camshaft lobe and cutting fuel pressure.",
                    "Cylinder Wall Scoring: The Alusil cylinder liners can score if oil changes are neglected or the engine is driven aggressively before reaching operating temperature.",
                    "Massive Oil Leaks: Valve cover gaskets and upper timing chain cover gaskets harden and leak oil profusely.",
                    "AVS Solenoid Failure: The Audi Valvelift System actuators on the cylinder head can fail, causing rough running and performance codes."
                ],
                vulnerabilities: [ 
                    "Catastrophic Timing Failure - A broken chain guide or skipped timing at the rear of the engine will destroy the valvetrain. Engine removal is required to fix this.",
                    "Cylinder Wall Scoring - Permanent damage to the Alusil engine block liners results in high oil consumption and eventually necessitates a full engine replacement.",
                    "Multitronic CVT Failure - Front-Wheel-Drive models are equipped with the 01J/0AW Multitronic CVT, which is highly prone to internal chain slippage and TCM failure.",
                    "Intake Choking (Carbon) - Neglecting carbon cleaning will eventually cause chunks of carbon to fall into the cylinders, scoring the walls or preventing valves from closing.",
                    "High-Pressure Fuel Pump Failure - If the HPFP fails internally, it can dilute the engine oil with raw gasoline, rapidly destroying engine bearings.",
                    "Engine Overheating - A stuck-closed thermostat (buried deep in the engine valley) can quickly warp the aluminum cylinder heads."
                ],
