                drivingExperience: "The 290hp CCAA 3.0 TFSI completely redefines the A6 C6. The supercharger provides instant, V8-like torque from idle with absolutely zero lag. It is a phenomenally fast and smooth powertrain that makes the heavy A6 feel incredibly athletic. It sounds fantastic, especially with an aftermarket intake that lets the supercharger whine be heard.",
                mechanicVerdict: "The 3.0 TFSI (EA837) is widely considered one of Audi's best engines of the 21st century. The block and internals are bulletproof. Yes, you have to deal with carbon buildup, and replacing the PCV/Thermostat under the supercharger is a chore, but it lacks the fatal flaws of the older NA V6s. It is an absolute tuning monster. Buy one, tune it to Stage 2, and embarrass modern sports cars.",
                repairCostEstimate: "$800 - $1600 / year (Carbon cleaning and PCV/Thermostat replacements are the main expenses)"
