                    "Multitronic CVT Failure - Front-Wheel-Drive models are equipped with the 01J Multitronic CVT, which is highly prone to internal chain slippage and TCM failure.",
                    "Intake Choking (Carbon) - Neglecting carbon cleaning will eventually cause chunks of carbon to fall into the cylinders, scoring the walls or preventing valves from closing.",
                    "High-Pressure Fuel Pump Failure - If the HPFP fails internally, it can dilute the engine oil with raw gasoline, rapidly destroying engine bearings.",
                    "Engine Overheating - A stuck-closed thermostat (buried deep in the engine valley) can quickly warp the aluminum cylinder heads."
