                timingType: "Chain (Highly complex rear-mounted timing chain system. Drives the camshafts and accessories from the rear of the engine block. Replacing the chains requires complete engine removal).", injectionType: "Direct Injection (FSI. Fuel is sprayed directly into the combustion chamber at up to 120 bar. Requires dual High-Pressure Fuel Pumps driven by the camshafts).", engineLifespan: "250,000+ km (The Alusil block is structurally strong, but the lifespan of the BVJ engine is dictated by its rear timing chain design, dual HPFP followers, and massive intake carbon buildup).", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. Features Audi Valvelift System (AVS) to broaden the torque curve).", ecuType: "Bosch Motronic MED9.1.1 (Dual ECUs managing the complex direct injection and AVS systems).", euroStandard: "Euro 4 / Euro 5", maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp (The rotating assembly is robust, but the engine bay thermal dynamics and Alusil block make forced induction extremely risky and rare).",
