                oilSpecification: "VW 502.00 5W-40",
                commonIssues: [ 
                    "Intake Manifold Flap Seizure: The internal plastic flaps of the variable intake manifold break or seize, causing rough idle and severe loss of low-end torque.",
                    "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: FSI direct injection leads to heavy carbon deposits on the intake valves, restricting airflow and causing cold-start misfires.",
                    "Rear Timing Chain Guide Failure: The plastic guides at the firewall shatter from extreme heat, causing the timing chain to rattle loudly on startup.",
                    "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: The twin cam-driven HPFP followers wear out and can damage the camshafts if not inspected regularly.",
                    "Massive Oil Leaks: Valve cover gaskets, oil filter housing gaskets, and timing cover gaskets leak profusely due to the intense V10 heat.",
                    "Ignition Coil Pack Failure: The extreme under-hood temperatures cause the ignition coils to crack and fail, resulting in sudden misfires."
                ],
                vulnerabilities: [ 
                    "The Engine Pull Tax - The V10 is packed so tightly that addressing the rear timing chain guides or major oil leaks requires completely dropping the engine and subframe.",
                    "Catastrophic Intake Disintegration - If the fragile plastic flaps inside the intake manifold break apart, pieces will be sucked into the cylinders, destroying the engine.",
                    "Cylinder Wall Scoring - The Alusil block lacks traditional iron liners; poor lubrication, dirty injectors, or overheating will permanently score the walls.",
                    "Transmission Torque Converter Failure - The ZF 6HP automatic transmission struggles with the heavy chassis and V10 torque, leading to lockup clutch failure.",
                    "Suspension Bushing Destruction - The massive weight of the 5.2L V10 hanging over the front axle rapidly destroys the front multi-link suspension bushings.",
                    "Catalytic Converter Meltdown - Unburned fuel from carbon-induced misfires will quickly overheat and melt the extremely expensive primary catalytic converters."
                ],
