                timingType: "Belt (Toothed timing belt driving the twin camshafts and water pump. Strict 120,000 km replacement interval. Features an updated gear-driven balance shaft module, but retains the flawed hex key).", injectionType: "Direct Injection (Pump Düse / PD. Camshaft-actuated unit injectors. Highly pressurized, providing strong torque but significant engine noise).", engineLifespan: "300,000+ km (The cast-iron block is incredibly tough. Audi fixed the snapping chains of the earlier models by using gears, but the oil pump hex key still rounds off, requiring proactive replacement for long life).", turboType: "Single Turbocharger (Garrett VNT. Variable Nozzle Turbine providing excellent mid-range punch, but prone to sticky vanes from soot, especially if a DPF is fitted).", ecuType: "Bosch EDC16U31 (Highly tuneable electronic diesel control).", euroStandard: "Euro 4", maxPowerStockInternals: "220+ hp (The block and forged crankshaft are very strong, but the factory turbo and clutch are the immediate bottlenecks).",
