                drivingExperience: "The 180hp BPP 2.7 V6 TDI is a masterclass in long-distance refinement. It lacks the explosive off-the-line surge of the 3.0 TDI, but it compensates with an incredibly smooth, linear power delivery that makes it feel more aristocratic. The V6 engine note is significantly more pleasant and less agricultural than the 4-cylinder TDI models. High-speed Autobahn stability is phenomenal, especially with Quattro, making it the perfect engine for someone who wants V6 smoothness without the full running costs of the 3.0 version.",
                mechanicVerdict: "The BPP is essentially a 'baby' 3.0 TDI and shares 90% of its DNA. It is a fantastic engine that can easily reach half a million kilometers if the Piezo injectors are strictly monitored. The biggest financial threats are the 'Engine-Out' rear timing chain service if the guides fail and the fragile Multitronic CVT on FWD models. Always buy a Quattro Tiptronic or a manual to ensure the drivetrain can handle the engine's long-term torque output. Proactive care is non-negotiable here.",
                repairCostEstimate: "$800 - $1800 / year (Standard maintenance is reasonable, but a single failing injector or timing chain guide will result in a $2000+ repair bill)"
