                timingType: "Chain (Highly complex rear-mounted timing chain system. Drives the camshafts and accessories. This facelift version features revised tensioners but still requires engine removal for full chain replacement).", injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection (Updated Bosch EDC17 with improved Piezoelectric injectors. Much more reliable than the early BPP versions).", engineLifespan: "450,000+ km (The pinnacle of the 2.7 TDI development. The block is indestructible, and the updated injection system makes it one of the most reliable V6 diesels ever produced).", turboType: "Single Turbocharger (Updated BorgWarner VNT. Features electronic actuator and optimized vane geometry for reduced lag and Euro 5 compliance).", ecuType: "Bosch EDC17CP14 (Highly advanced, allows for precise injection events and excellent tuning potential).", euroStandard: "Euro 5", maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (Structurally identical to the 3.0 TDI models, meaning the engine block is virtually unburstable).",
                fuelConsumption: { city: "9.0 - 10.2 L/100km", highway: "5.5 - 6.8 L/100km", mixed: "6.8 - 7.8 L/100km", sporty: "11.0+ L/100km" },
                oilSpecification: "VW 507.00 5W-30",
