                    "Glow Plug Pressure Sensor Failure: Specific glow plugs on the CANA feature integrated cylinder pressure sensors which are extremely expensive and fail often.",
                    "EGR Valve Sooting: The updated Euro 5 EGR system recirculates more soot, leading to faster carbon accumulation in the intake manifold.",
                    "Oil Cooler Seals: The seals for the oil cooler in the engine valley can leak, causing oil and coolant to mix or leak down the back of the block.",
                    "Throttle Body Actuator Strip: Plastic gears inside the throttle body (anti-shudder valve) strip out, preventing smooth shutdown."
