    id: "cvkb-a6-c7", brand: "Audi", model: "A6", generation: "C7 (2011-2018)", engineCode: "CVKB", profileId: "cvkb-a6-c7", displacement: "1,984 cc", power: "190 hp (140 kW)", torque: "320 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 4, valves: 16, compression: "11.7:1", yearRange: "2015-2018",
    timingType: "Chain (EA888 Gen 3B 'B-Cycle' architecture. Highly reliable timing chain and tensioner system, though standard high-mileage monitoring is still recommended).", injectionType: "Dual Injection (Combines Direct Injection FSI with Multi-Point Injection MPI. Keeps the intake valves clean and optimizes the unique Miller-cycle combustion process).", engineLifespan: "300,000+ km (An efficiency-focused masterpiece. Experiences very little thermal or mechanical stress compared to the 252hp models, ensuring extreme longevity if cooling components are maintained).", turboType: "Single Turbocharger (Specifically sized for efficiency and rapid spooling at low RPMs to complement the high-compression Miller cycle).", ecuType: "Siemens Simos 18.1 (Highly sophisticated, meticulously calibrated to manage the complex valve timing and high compression ratio of the B-cycle).", euroStandard: "Euro 6", maxPowerStockInternals: "320+ hp (While the block is strong, the very high 11.7:1 compression ratio limits extreme high-boost tuning compared to the standard 9.6:1 Gen 3 models).",
    fuelConsumption: { city: "7.0 - 8.0 L/100km", highway: "4.5 - 5.5 L/100km", mixed: "5.5 - 6.5 L/100km", sporty: "9.0+ L/100km" },
    oilSpecification: "VW 508.00 0W-20",
    commonIssues: [ 
        "Thermostat & Water Pump Housing Leaks: The plastic housing inevitably warps and cracks under constant thermal cycling, causing slow but persistent coolant loss.",
        "PCV Valve Failure: The delicate internal rubber diaphragm tears, leading to vacuum leaks, rough idle, whistling noises, and increased crankcase pressure.",
        "Turbocharger Wastegate Rattle: The electronic actuator rod develops play over time, leading to a metallic rattle on deceleration and potential underboost codes.",
        "Ignition Coil Failure: Frequent failure of factory coil packs, especially prominent if the vehicle is tuned.",
        "Oil Pan Leaks: The factory plastic oil pan is highly susceptible to cracking from road debris or warping if drain plug torque is exceeded.",
        "S Tronic Mechatronic Wear: The DL382 7-speed dual-clutch transmission can experience harsh shifting or mechatronic failure if 60,000 km fluid changes are ignored."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [ 
        "Catastrophic Overheating - The plastic water pump module can fail suddenly, rapidly dumping coolant and warping the aluminum cylinder head before the driver notices.",
        "Rear Main Seal Blowout - A failed PCV valve permanently pressurizes the engine crankcase, which eventually blows out the rear main seal, causing massive oil leaks.",
        "Turbocharger Seizure - If the electronic wastegate actuator fails completely or oil feed lines clog with degraded oil, the turbocharger will overspin and self-destruct.",
        "Transmission Destruction - The 7-speed S Tronic gearbox will suffer catastrophic clutch pack and mechatronic failure without strict fluid and filter services.",
        "Detonation/Knock - Because of the high 11.7:1 compression ratio, using low-octane fuel or running a poor aggressive tune will cause severe engine knock and shatter the piston ring lands.",
        "Coolant Migration - Defective coolant temperature sensors can leak coolant internally into the wiring harness, migrating all the way to the ECU and destroying it."
    ],
