    timingType: "Chain (EA837 architecture. Features a complex rear-mounted timing chain system. Upper tensioners can be accessed with difficulty, but addressing stretched lower chains or shattered guides requires pulling the engine entirely).", injectionType: "Direct Injection (FSI. Highly susceptible to severe carbon buildup on the intake valves, severely choking airflow and reducing power output over time).", engineLifespan: "350,000+ km (The aluminum block is very durable. Lifespan is largely determined by maintaining the complex timing chains, regular walnut blasting, and transmission health).", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. Relies purely on displacement and Audi Valvelift System for power delivery).", ecuType: "Siemens Simos 8.x (Reliable engine management, though tuning potential is practically nonexistent due to the lack of forced induction).", euroStandard: "Euro 5", maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (Internals are robust, but naturally aspirated limitations mean you will never reach these limits without adding a custom supercharger).",
    fuelConsumption: { city: "10.5 - 12.0 L/100km", highway: "6.5 - 7.8 L/100km", mixed: "8.0 - 9.5 L/100km", sporty: "13.0+ L/100km" },
    oilSpecification: "VW 502.00 5W-40",
    commonIssues: [ 
        "Severe Carbon Buildup: Direct injection without port washing leads to thick, baked-on carbon on the intake valves, causing cold start misfires and huge power loss.",
        "Rear Timing Chain Rattle: The plastic guides and hydraulic tensioners at the rear of the engine fail, causing a loud rattle on startup.",
        "Valve Cover Gasket Leaks: The plastic valve covers warp and the gaskets harden, leaking oil directly onto the hot exhaust manifolds.",
        "PCV Valve Failure: The internal diaphragm fails, causing excessive crankcase pressure, massive vacuum leaks, and a loud whistling noise.",
        "High-Pressure Fuel Pump Wear: The cam-driven HPFP can fail or leak, diluting engine oil with gasoline.",
        "Thermostat Failure: The thermostat often gets stuck open, preventing the engine from reaching operating temperature and ruining fuel economy."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [ 
        "The Engine Pull Tax - The timing chain system is located at the rear of the engine. If the lower guides shatter, the entire engine and transmission must be removed for a multi-thousand-dollar repair.",
        "Airflow Choking (Carbon) - If left uncleaned, carbon buildup will become so severe that pieces can break off, damaging valve seats and completely destroying performance.",
        "Multitronic CVT Destruction - FWD models use the fragile 0AW Multitronic CVT. The internal chain slips and the TCM fails, requiring a complete, extremely expensive rebuild.",
        "S Tronic Mechatronic Failure - Quattro models use the DL501 7-speed DSG. Neglecting 60k km fluid changes will destroy the mechatronics and dual clutch pack.",
        "Catalytic Converter Failure - Oil leaking from the valve covers or excessive unburned fuel from carbon-induced misfires will quickly ruin the primary catalytic converters.",
        "Bore Scoring - Poor quality fuel and neglected oil changes can lead to scoring of the Alusil cylinder walls, requiring a new engine block."
    ],
