    timingType: "Belt (EA288 generation architecture. Toothed timing belt driving the camshafts and the high-pressure fuel pump. The water pump is integrated into the block. Strict 210,000 km replacement interval, but the tensioner is prone to squeaking early).", injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection (Utilizes the more reliable Bosch CP4.1 generation with improved materials, though still sensitive to poor fuel).", engineLifespan: "400,000+ km (The EA288 is a massive improvement over the EA189. Being a detuned version, this engine experiences incredibly low thermal stress, ensuring maximum block longevity).", turboType: "Single Turbocharger (BorgWarner VNT. Features a water-cooled intercooler integrated directly into the intake manifold for incredibly short intake tracts and rapid response).", ecuType: "Bosch EDC17C64 (Heavily detuned via software for corporate fleet and tax bracket restrictions in certain markets).", euroStandard: "Euro 6", maxPowerStockInternals: "240+ hp (The block is bulletproof, structurally identical to the 150hp and 190hp variants).",
    fuelConsumption: { city: "5.4 - 6.4 L/100km", highway: "3.9 - 4.9 L/100km", mixed: "4.7 - 5.4 L/100km", sporty: "6.8+ L/100km" },
    oilSpecification: "VW 507.00 5W-30",
    commonIssues: [ 
        "Switchable Water Pump Failure: The mechanical sliding shroud on the water pump gets stuck, causing the engine to overheat suddenly or take forever to warm up.",
        "Heater Core Blockage (Silica Gel): The 'Silikat' bag inside the coolant expansion tank bursts, sending silica beads through the cooling system and permanently blocking the heater matrix.",
        "Timing Belt Tensioner Squeak: The timing belt tensioner bearing dries out and squeaks loudly on cold starts, requiring early timing belt replacement.",
        "Dual EGR Valve Sooting: The complex dual EGR system (High and Low pressure) is highly prone to clogging with soot, especially on cars used exclusively for short trips.",
        "DPF Pressure Sensor Failure: The differential pressure sensor fails frequently, throwing false 'DPF Clogged' codes.",
        "Dual Mass Flywheel (DMF) Wear: The heavy diesel torque spikes weaken the DMF springs over time, causing severe vibrations at idle."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [ 
        "Catastrophic Overheating - If the switchable water pump shroud sticks in the closed position, the engine will overheat in minutes, risking a warped cylinder head.",
        "Heater Core Destruction (Silica) - Once the silica bag bursts in the expansion tank, the heater core is ruined. Replacing it requires removing the entire dashboard.",
        "DPF Regeneration Failure - If the EGR system clogs or the pressure sensor fails, the DPF will not regenerate, leading to a permanent blockage and turbo damage.",
        "Valvetrain Damage (Timing Belt) - Ignoring the tensioner squeak can eventually lead to tensioner failure, causing the belt to jump and pistons to smash the valves.",
        "Transmission Destruction - The 7-speed S Tronic DL382 gearbox will suffer catastrophic clutch pack and mechatronic failure without strict 60,000 km fluid services.",
        "Sensor Glow Plug Breakage - Euro 6 emissions require expensive cylinder pressure sensing glow plugs. If they break during removal, the cylinder head must be removed."
    ],
