    mechanicVerdict: "The CLAA is a detuned version of the mighty 3.0 TDI, meaning it shares the exact same robust hardware but operates under far less stress. This makes it an absolute steal for tuning. However, it still suffers from the massive V6 TDI flaws: the terrifying CP4.2 fuel pump failure, oil cooler leaks in the engine valley, and timing chain rattle. Most importantly, if this engine is attached to a FWD Multitronic CVT, you must avoid tuning it entirely, as the transmission will self-destruct under the increased torque. If it is Quattro (DSG), tune away.",
