        "Bosch CP4.2 HPFP Failure: The twin-plunger High-Pressure Fuel Pump internals wear rapidly if fuel lubricity is low, sending catastrophic metal shavings through the entire fuel system.",
        "Upper Timing Chain Rattle: The hydraulic tensioners for the upper camshaft chains lose oil pressure overnight, causing a loud 1-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts.",
        "Oil Cooler Seals: The seals for the oil cooler located deep in the engine V-valley leak, causing oil and coolant to mix or leak down the back of the block.",
