    drivingExperience: "The 272hp CRTD is widely considered the peak diesel engine for the A6 C7. It provides a relentless, effortless wave of 580 Nm torque that pins you to your seat with virtually zero turbo lag. It pulls the heavy chassis with shocking urgency, yet remains whisper-quiet and incredibly refined at 160 km/h on the highway. Paired with the rear-biased Quattro system and the lightning-fast DL501 DSG, it is a masterclass in combining supreme comfort, excellent fuel economy, and genuine sports-sedan pace.",
    mechanicVerdict: "The CRTD is a phenomenal powerhouse, but it is heavily burdened by the Euro 6 AdBlue (SCR) system. While the iron block is indestructible, you are battling the CP4 fuel pump, timing chain rattle, AND the highly fragile AdBlue pumps/NOx sensors, which can literally prevent the car from starting if they fail. If you buy this car, you must protect the fuel pump with additives and keep a repair fund ready for the emissions equipment. It is an incredible, highly tunable machine, but it demands meticulous care.",
